<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no">
    <meta name="description" content="Explore shipping support across the United States, Australia, the United Kingdom, New Zealand, and other international routes.">
    <title>Service Locations | <%= business.name %></title>
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/png" href="/images/img/favicon.png">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com/" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;400;500;600;700;800&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/slicknav.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/all.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/custom.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="/css/content-pages.css" rel="stylesheet">
<link href="/css/brand.css" rel="stylesheet">
<%- include('../partials/chat') %>
<link href="/css/zoom.css" rel="stylesheet">
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('../partials/site-header') %>
    <div class="page-header"><div class="container"><div class="page-header-box"><h2>Service Locations</h2><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li>Locations</li></ol></nav></div></div></div>

    <main class="content-page">
        <div class="container">
            <section class="content-intro">
                <div class="content-kicker">Where we operate</div>
                <h1>Connecting your shipments with global markets</h1>
                <p>Our carrier and service partner network helps coordinate freight, delivery, customs, project cargo, and pet transport across domestic and international routes.</p>
            </section>

            <div class="locations-grid">
                <article class="location-card"><div class="location-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-flag-usa" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h2>United States</h2><p>Support for domestic and international shipments through major US commercial hubs, ports, airports, and delivery networks.</p></article>
                <article class="location-card"><div class="location-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-earth-oceania" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h2>Australia</h2><p>Planning and destination coordination for imports, exports, interstate freight, and specialist shipments in Australia.</p></article>
                <article class="location-card"><div class="location-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-bridge" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h2>United Kingdom</h2><p>Air, sea, road, customs, and final-delivery coordination for commercial and personal shipments across the UK.</p></article>
                <article class="location-card"><div class="location-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-compass" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h2>New Zealand</h2><p>Import, export, pet travel, and delivery support through New Zealand’s main transport gateways.</p></article>
                <article class="location-card location-card-global"><div class="location-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-globe" aria-hidden="true"></i></div><h2>Global Coverage</h2><p>We also review routes beyond these markets with international carriers and local partners. Availability depends on the cargo, origin, destination, applicable requirements, capacity, and schedule.</p></article>
            </div>

            <section class="coverage-note"><div><h2>Shipping somewhere else?</h2><p>Tell us where your shipment is going, what you’re moving, and when it needs to arrive. We’ll review the available route options.</p></div><a href="contact.html" class="btn-default">Explore Your Route</a></section>
        </div>
    </main>

    <%- include('../partials/site-footer') %>
    
    <script src="/js/jquery-3.7.1.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/jquery.slicknav.js"></script>
    <script src="/js/service-navigation.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
